#include <mma.h>
using namespace nvcuda;

// ===========================================================================
// qr_trailing_resident: PERSISTENT-CTA A-RESIDENT trailing update (n=512/1024).
//
// THE BRIEF'S DELIVERABLE. The Triton fused trailing (_trailing_fused_kernel)
// reads the A column-strip TWICE per outer block: sweep1 W=V^T@A reads A, sweep2
// A-=V@(T^T W) RE-READS the same A. Both reads miss L1 (~0.16% L1 hit, ncu) so
// the kernel is long_scoreboard (L1-miss->L2 latency) bound (33-39% of stalls),
// NOT bandwidth bound (DRAM 24%). A Triton A-resident strip was tried + rejected
// as pathological (94539us) so the A-residency MUST be a hand-written CUDA kernel
// with EXPLICIT smem staging -- this kernel.
//
// Grid = (col_tiles, B). Each CTA OWNS one matrix's A column-strip
// Cs[pheight x BNc] for the WHOLE outer block (all BLK reflectors): it loads the
// strip from H into SMEM ONCE, does BOTH sweeps against the resident smem strip
// (W=V^T@Cs_smem, then Cs_smem -= V@W'), and writes the strip back ONCE. So the
// strip touches HBM/L2 once-read + once-write instead of twice-read+once-write,
// and sweep2's A access hits SMEM (~30cyc) instead of L1-miss->L2 (~200cyc),
// directly cutting the long_scoreboard stall. V stays in GLOBAL (it is 512x32=64KB
// per matrix -- staging it too would blow the smem budget; the "V re-read per
// col-tile" cost is unchanged and is a separate, smaller lever).
//
// GEMMs are tf32x3 error-corrected WMMA (m16n16k8): a=a_hi+a_lo (a_hi=tf32(a),
// a_lo=tf32(a-a_hi)); a*b ~= a_hi*b_hi + a_hi*b_lo + a_lo*b_hi (3 MMAs recover
// ~fp32 from tf32 HW). tensor cores are MANDATORY (a prior measurement found the
// FP32-CUDA-core smem trailing 5x slower). Adapted from qr_la_trailing_tc
// (commit 0dab5261, leaderboard-accepted) but with Cs RESIDENT in smem.
//
// RISK (measured, not assumed): a (pheight x BNc) resident smem strip is large
// (n=512,BNc=32 -> 64KB) so it caps blocks/SM HARD (~1-2), LOWER than the Triton
// fused's 6 blocks/SM. Less occupancy = less latency hiding. The bet is the
// smem-hit A access removes more stall than the lost occupancy adds. If it loses,
// that is a CLEAN NEGATIVE confirming the n=512 trailing is at its structural
// floor.
//
// Smem layout (dynamic): sCs[ pheight x BNc ] col-major (the resident A strip,
// padded rows to a multiple of 16 for WMMA frag alignment) followed by
// sW[ BLK x BNc ] (W then W'' reuse) col-major (ldm BLK).
// Contract: V is the CLEAN reflector panel in Vbuf (Vt layout: Vt[k, r] at
// Vbuf[bid*svb + k*svk + r*svn]), with Vt[k,r]=1 if r==(j+k), =reflector if
// r>(j+k), else 0 -- i.e. V[r,k] (col-major (pheight x BLK)) = Vt[k, j+r].
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
